## Context

Promotion requested by the author (padme native-note triage, 2026-11-07; padme
smelt report `memory/smelts/2026-11-07-first-skill-smelt.md`). The Claude Code
native note `feedback_languages.md` in padme's project store says: bash for
mechanistic system scripts (monitoring, backups); Python for anything calling
an LLM API or handling complex data, because bash JSON encoding broke on
multilingual text; Rust reserved for high-frequency infrastructure loops
(startup time). No harness rule says when to leave bash.

## Destination

`rules/coding-bash.md`, a new short section on when a script should not be
bash. Wording is the harness's call.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `rules/coding-bash.md` states the language split (bash / Python for LLM
  calls and structured data / Rust for high-frequency loops), with the JSON
  encoding failure as its reason.
